Umbriel and its portal aren't in Arch's repositories or the AUR yet, so
install.sh builds them from these PKGBUILDs when you pick Umbriel
(packages umbriel-git and xdg-desktop-portal-umbriel-git, which pacman
can remove like any other).

Each is pinned to the commit Material3UI was tested with (_commit), since
Umbriel changes as it's developed. To move to a newer Umbriel: build it,
check the shell in it (docs/UMBRIEL.md), then set _commit (and the
portal's, built the same day) to the tested commits and run
  ./install.sh --compositor umbriel
again. Once Umbriel is packaged upstream, the installer takes that
package instead.
